environ
	 Batch sizes, in processor order. Measured on the node (8x A100) on 2026-11-17
	DOWNLOAD_BATCH_SIZE 64	 Images per run of download_image. Network bound: 1.5 MB per PNG
	SPLIT_BATCH_SIZE 64	     Images per run of split_alpha. CPU only: it reads 1 PNG and writes 2
	ENCODE_BATCH_SIZE 128	 Images per run of encode_latents (about 40 s on one A100). run_proc_curate.fish starts two loops per GPU
	COLORBG_BATCH_SIZE 512	 Images per run of encode_colorbg. Big: a run costs ~40 s besides the encoding. run_proc_colorbg.fish starts 1 loop per GPU
	TRIMASK_BATCH_SIZE 512	        Images per run of each trimask_<method>. CPU only: it reads 1 PNG and writes 1 per variant. run_proc_trimask.fish starts 2 loops per method
	TRIMASK_ENCODE_BATCH_SIZE 1024	 Trimasks per run of encode_trimask: big, so the ~40 s per-run cost is shared. run_proc_trimask.fish starts two loops per GPU

	 Data
	MAGICK_REPO OneOverZero/MAGICK	 Hugging Face dataset: 140,955 RGBA PNGs, 1024 x 1024, straight alpha, 191 GB
	GRAY_LEVEL 0.5	                 Background of rgb_on_gray as a fraction of white: rgb * alpha + GRAY_LEVEL * (1 - alpha)
	EVAL_MODULUS 4000	             An image is eval, never trained on, when sha256(page_id) mod EVAL_MODULUS is 0: about 35 images

	 Models
	TEACHER_MODEL Efficient-Large-Model/SANA_Sprint_1.6B_1024px_teacher_diffusers	 The model we fine-tune. Its vae subfolder (DC-AE f32c32) makes the latents, so they match the model
	TEACHER_DIR ../models/Sana_Sprint_1.6B_1024px_teacher_diffusers	                 TEACHER_MODEL on FSx. encode_latents copies it to /models/sana-sprint-alpha-incontext once per machine

	 Eval (plan_eval, generate_eval)
	EVAL_SET resources/eval	 Eval images, captions and fixed noise, relative to the repo root. src/sana_alpha/eval_set.py makes it. Default of eval_models.eval_set
	EVAL_BATCH_SIZE 16	      eval_generations rows per run of generate_eval. A run costs ~12 s besides the GPU: 8 rows took 15 s

	 Trimask augmentations (trimask_<method>, manifest §13)
	TRIMASK_SUBSET 012	 A method uses a train image when the first hex digit of sha256(page_id + method) is one of these: about 26k images
	TRIMASK_VARIANTS 1	 Trimasks per image and method

	 Database
	DATABASE_PORT 23947	 Far from the ports of the Bluejay demos on the laptop (19471, 19683, 19783)

database
	backend bluejay.local_database.LocalLanceBackend
	host 0.0.0.0
	port $DATABASE_PORT
	root lance

claims_table bluejay_claims
runs_table bluejay_runs
lineage_table bluejay_lineage
lineage true


 RULES FOR MAINTAINING THIS DTAB (copied from MulticamDailies' project.dtab, the house style):
 SEMANTIC BINDING: dtab-rules
    - One tab renders as four spaces. After each edit run: python3 agents/dtab_format.py check data/project.dtab (fix repairs the columns)
    - Formatting is part of the interface. Copy the alignment of nearby blocks exactly. Do not reformat what the user aligned by hand
    - These rules are for the AI. Keep the user's own prose in the user's voice: do not rewrite it
    - Everything is written in ASD-STE100
    - Sort tables and processors by dependency: an item comes after each item that it reads
    - Put the primary key first, then group the columns by the processor that writes them
    - Give each committed column a TYPE, a DESCRIPTION and an EXAMPLE
    - [Key] identifies a primary key. A tilde immediately before the type identifies a materialized field copied unchanged to the commit output,
      with no other use by the processor, including diagnostic logging.
    - Annotate each corresponding materialize and commit row that exists in the DTAB. Replace the space before the type with ~, as in [Key] ~str,
      without moving the columns. Preserve at least one space after the comment tab; widen the table if necessary. The marker is part of the comment, not the field name.
    - Write each processor's query inline in the processor. The queries section holds only queries for Sparrow
    - Delete a query that no processor or widget uses
    - Delete a processor file that this dtab does not use, in its own commit
    - Remove a note when it is resolved
    - Right-align values at their shared suffix, like numbers at the decimal point: ` 720p.mp4` under `1080p.mp4`
    - Lay out a big query's SELECT like view_dataset: one item per line, struct fields aligned
    - Write each query that is not tiny and simple as an annotated SQL query, like encode_latents' query, for a reader who does not speak SQL.
      An annotated SQL query has these properties in its FROM, JOIN and WHERE:
        - Break lines where the English breaks: each line is one short statement. Join lines that make one statement, like SELECT ... FROM
        - End each line with a tiny -- comment, so that the comments read down as one sentence
        - Align the comments one space after the longest line. Inside parentheses, indent the comment text 4 more, so the reader can skip it
        - Align the parts that nearby lines share, such as AND, IS, ON and =
    - Eval inference runs here as generate_eval (user, m00606, m00611). Judging the results is done by the agent (m00371)


tables

	bluejay_claims
		 Bluejay requires this table
		primary_key claim_id
		index	claim_id btree
		columns
			claim_id, run_id, claim_status string

	bluejay_runs
		 Bluejay requires this table
		primary_key run_id
		columns
			run_id, run_status, started_at, finished_at, processor, metadata, dtab, query string
			exit_code int64
			log blob
			profiler blob

	bluejay_lineage
		 Bluejay requires this table, because lineage is true
		columns
			claim_id, table string
			key, materialized map_(string(), binary())
			committed list_(string())

	import_jobs
		 One seeded row makes import_index read magick_index.tsv exactly once
		primary_key job_id
		columns
			job_id string
			index_tsv blob
		initial_rows
			,	job_id magick

	magick_samples
		 One row per MAGICK image: 140,955 rows when the download is done
		primary_key page_id
		columns
			page_id string

			 Written by import_index, from magick_index.tsv
			subject, color, split, source_claim_id, source_run_id string
			sim_score float64
			nsfw, hand_picked bool

			 Written by download_image
			rgba blob

			 Written by split_alpha
			alpha, rgb_on_gray blob
			alpha_coverage, alpha_soft_fraction, green_spill float64

			 Written by encode_latents
			latent_alpha_1024, latent_rgb_1024 blob
			vae_psnr_1024 float64

			 Written by encode_colorbg, for adapter_v2
			bg_color list_(float32(), 3)
			latent_rgb_colorbg_1024 blob

	eval_models
		 One row per model to evaluate. To evaluate a new checkpoint, add a row here: run_proc_eval.fish initializes first
		primary_key model_tag
		columns
			model_tag, pipeline, checkpoint, prompt_variant, eval_set string	 Empty eval_set = EVAL_SET
			steps int64
			guidance float64
		initial_rows
			,
				model_tag sprint_plain
				pipeline sprint
				checkpoint stock
				prompt_variant plain
				steps 2
				guidance 4.5
			,
				model_tag sprint_gray
				pipeline sprint
				checkpoint stock
				prompt_variant gray
				steps 2
				guidance 4.5
			,
				model_tag teacher_plain
				pipeline teacher
				checkpoint stock
				prompt_variant plain
				steps 20
				guidance 4.5
			,
				model_tag teacher_gray
				pipeline teacher
				checkpoint stock
				prompt_variant gray
				steps 20
				guidance 4.5
			,
				model_tag adapter_toy_ddp2_step000400
				pipeline teacher
				checkpoint models/adapter/toy_ddp2/step_000400
				prompt_variant plain
				steps 20
				guidance 4.5
			,
				model_tag control_overfit_test_step000400
				pipeline teacher
				checkpoint models/control/overfit_test/step_000400
				prompt_variant plain
				steps 20
				guidance 4.5
			,
				model_tag final_overfit_test_step000400
				pipeline teacher
				checkpoint models/control/overfit_test/final_step_000400
				prompt_variant plain
				steps 20
				guidance 4.5
			,
				 Step 5 transfer: a control step on the sprint pipeline = stock student + merged control LoRA + gates
				model_tag transfer_overfit_test_step000400_1step
				pipeline sprint
				checkpoint models/control/overfit_test/step_000400
				prompt_variant plain
				steps 1
				guidance 4.5
			,
				model_tag transfer_overfit_test_step000400_2step
				pipeline sprint
				checkpoint models/control/overfit_test/step_000400
				prompt_variant plain
				steps 2
				guidance 4.5
			,
				model_tag transfer_overfit_test_step000400_4step
				pipeline sprint
				checkpoint models/control/overfit_test/step_000400
				prompt_variant plain
				steps 4
				guidance 4.5
			,
				 Step 2: the real adapter run
				model_tag adapter_v1_step001000
				pipeline teacher
				checkpoint models/adapter/adapter_v1/step_001000
				prompt_variant plain
				steps 20
				guidance 4.5
			,
				 The adapter that control_v1 is trained on
				model_tag adapter_v1_step002000
				pipeline teacher
				checkpoint models/adapter/adapter_v1/step_002000
				prompt_variant plain
				steps 20
				guidance 4.5
			,
				 Step 3, 4 and 5 of control_v1 step 500: control on the adapter, final (no adapter), and transfer onto Sprint
				model_tag control_v1_step000500
				pipeline teacher
				checkpoint models/control/control_v1/step_000500
				prompt_variant plain
				steps 20
				guidance 4.5
			,
				model_tag final_v1_step000500
				pipeline teacher
				checkpoint models/control/control_v1/final_step_000500
				prompt_variant plain
				steps 20
				guidance 4.5
			,
				model_tag transfer_v1_step000500_2step
				pipeline sprint
				checkpoint models/control/control_v1/step_000500
				prompt_variant plain
				steps 2
				guidance 4.5
			,
				 The final model lost the gray background. Fixes tried: the gray prompt, and keeping part of the adapter (λ)
